# Day 25/60 — AI Shark Tank Simulator

## Objective

Today I explored startup pitching by simulating an investment meeting using Claude.

The goal was to evaluate a startup idea through AI investors, answer challenging business questions, and understand how investors assess opportunities before making funding decisions.

---

## What Was Generated

- AI Shark Tank Simulation
- Investor Question & Answer Session
- Startup Investment Scorecard
- Funding Recommendation
- Valuation Analysis
- Investment Decision Report
- Startup Leaderboard
- Downloadable Pitch Report

---

## What I Learned

### Investors Evaluate More Than Ideas

A great idea alone isn't enough.

Investors also evaluate execution, market opportunity, competition, business model, and founder capability.

### Every Question Reveals a Weakness

The toughest investor questions often uncover assumptions that founders overlook.

Preparing answers improves both the product and the business.

### AI Creates a Safe Practice Environment

Claude simulated realistic investor feedback, making it easier to refine the pitch before presenting it to real people.

### Feedback Is Valuable

Constructive criticism is often more useful than immediate approval.

